WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.063
Curio tests your explanations through a
simulated learner.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.771
Choose a lesson on seasons. This offline demo
uses scripted model responses.

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.616
The session opens its concept map and evidence.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.891
A sample explanation wrongly blames summer on
distance from the Sun. The claim ledger records
the problem.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.677
The teacher corrects that claim, but leaves
daylight unexplained. The map updates, and
uncertainty stays visible.

6
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.803
Finishing the session produces a teach-back from
the recorded explanation.

7
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.395
The report preserves what the learner
understood, including the remaining gap.

8
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.595
The learner account keeps that uncertainty
visible.

9
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.035
After a real server restart, the saved report
reloads with no new model calls.

10
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.071
A separate reference tab shows the complete
explanation.

11
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.229
Human review keeps the unresolved claim and its
transcript evidence together.

12
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:14.457
Finally, the original session reopens with its
saved transcript. Voice would need reconnecting;
earlier questions are not replayed.
